1
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:08,282
BootWeave helps QNX developers review startup changes before they reach a device.

2
00:00:08,317 --> 00:00:12,958
One extra configuration dependency can tie an essential controller to optional telemetry.

3
00:00:12,993 --> 00:00:18,775
We make that relationship visible and give code review and continuous integration an explainable check.

4
00:00:19,713 --> 00:00:22,002
This is our authored three-service workload.

5
00:00:22,037 --> 00:00:27,018
The software sensor serves native QNX messages, the controller reads samples,

6
00:00:27,053 --> 00:00:31,666
and telemetry is optional. Change review keeps baseline and candidate files independent.

7
00:00:31,701 --> 00:00:36,202
Compare the revised baseline with the risky candidate and protect the controller.

8
00:00:36,237 --> 00:00:41,846
The policy rejects the new session coupling and shows the exact path and changed dependency.

9
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,804
Swap the revisions to review the correction.

10
00:00:45,839 --> 00:00:50,121
Removing the unnecessary telemetry prerequisite passes the same protected-service policy.

11
00:00:50,156 --> 00:00:54,018
Source fingerprints and property differences keep the decision reviewable.

12
00:00:54,053 --> 00:00:56,659
Static coupling remains a configuration model;

13
00:00:56,694 --> 00:00:59,718
the graph does not simulate a restart.

14
00:01:00,647 --> 00:01:07,462
We cross-compiled these C services with the QNX toolchain and ran them on QNX 8.0

15
00:01:07,497 --> 00:01:12,999
in QEMU with KVM. A separate host receiver captured
process instances and successful message-passing counters.

16
00:01:13,034 --> 00:01:20,772
In the risky automatic-failure experiment, killing telemetry caused SLM
to replace telemetry and the controller. The sensor stayed unchanged.

17
00:01:21,713 --> 00:01:27,152
In the revised experiment, telemetry restarted while the
controller kept its instance and continued successful

18
00:01:27,187 --> 00:01:30,121
sensor IPC in the observed windows.

19
00:01:30,156 --> 00:01:34,164
Imported recordings are checked against the exact XML hash.

20
00:01:34,199 --> 00:01:38,564
A match does not authenticate their origin or prove a fresh execution.

21
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:41,891
Switch configurations and the check is cleared or rejected.

22
00:01:41,926 --> 00:01:44,503
Static analysis and recorded observations stay separate.

23
00:01:45,447 --> 00:01:49,636
Cycles and missing prerequisites cannot pass as clean results.

24
00:01:49,671 --> 00:01:53,406
We also captured scoped native checks for modules,

25
00:01:53,441 --> 00:01:59,720
readiness, and include handling. BootWeave rejects
unsupported includes rather than silently skipping them.

26
00:01:59,755 --> 00:02:03,490
An operation-specific SLM discrepancy remains documented.

27
00:02:03,525 --> 00:02:07,987
These experiments make no availability, timing, or safety-certification claim.

28
00:02:08,913 --> 00:02:12,234
Export the review bundle with its static report,

29
00:02:12,269 --> 00:02:17,854
recording, and binding result. The host product needs only Python and a browser.

30
00:02:17,889 --> 00:02:21,331
The MIT-licensed repository includes native source, raw evidence,

31
00:02:21,366 --> 00:02:23,595
CI checks, and a tutorial.

32
00:02:23,630 --> 00:02:29,377
BootWeave turns a hidden lifecycle relationship into a reviewable change and a reproducible experiment.

